# The configuration of ferund (ferund.service), as environment variables:
# every flag of `ferund serve` has one, FERUN_ and the flag's name in upper
# snake case (--database-url: FERUN_DATABASE_URL); `ferund serve --help`
# lists them with their defaults. The file is readable by root and the
# group ferun alone: it holds the database's password.
#
#   FERUN_DATABASE_URL          the PostgreSQL DSN, required: PostgreSQL 17
#                               or newer, with synchronous replication when
#                               it has replicas.
#   FERUN_LISTEN                the front doors (REST, MCP, the UI, the
#                               ports), plain HTTP behind the HTTPS
#                               balancer, :8100 by default; with
#                               FERUN_TLS_CERT and FERUN_TLS_KEY, HTTPS.
#   FERUN_NODE_LISTEN           the nodes' port, TLS 1.3, :7443 by default.
#   FERUN_NODE_ADVERTISE_ADDRESS
#                               host:port at which nodes reach this
#                               instance's nodes' port; every instance of
#                               several sets it. Empty, the nodes reach the
#                               instance only by the name they were
#                               configured with: one machine.
#   FERUN_TRUST_DOMAIN          the SPIFFE trust domain, feos.local by
#                               default; the nodes' --trust-domain.
#   FERUN_CA_DIR                the issuer: issuer.crt, issuer.key,
#                               issuer.json and bundle.crt from
#                               `ferund init-ca`, /etc/ferun/ca by default.
#                               issuer.key must be readable by the group
#                               ferun; the root's key is never here.
#   FERUN_PUBLIC_URL            the front door's external URL, such as
#                               https://run.example.com; required with
#                               FERUN_OIDC_ISSUER.
#   FERUN_OIDC_ISSUER           human sign-in with OIDC; needs
#                               FERUN_PUBLIC_URL and
#   FERUN_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET_FILE,
#                               with FERUN_OIDC_CLIENT_ID (ferun by default)
#                               and FERUN_OIDC_ADMIN_GROUP (admins by
#                               default).
#   FERUN_ADMIN_USERS           user:password,... for the admin API and the
#                               UI, beside or instead of OIDC.
#   FERUN_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN       a token of the tenant operator, made while
#                               no tenant exists.
#   FERUN_SHUTDOWN_GRACE        how long a stopping instance finishes its
#                               requests and ops, 10m by default. The unit's
#                               TimeoutStopSec is this plus 30 s: a longer
#                               grace needs a drop-in that raises it.
#
# A single machine, with PostgreSQL beside it:
#
#   FERUN_DATABASE_URL=postgres://ferun:secret@127.0.0.1:5432/ferun?sslmode=disable
#   FERUN_TRUST_DOMAIN=run.example.com
#   FERUN_ADMIN_USERS=admin:secret
FERUN_DATABASE_URL=
